      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4324",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}$. Given that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$, find the value of $t$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular) if and only if $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot t \\\\  & =-8-10+t \\\\  & =t-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ t-18 & =0 \\\\ t & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
