        ":question/id": "7db3af69-69b0-5a51-a3ca-bf5d1a73cdb2",
        ":question/problem": "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}4{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-10)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8{r}^{2}-4{r}^{2}-30 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2}-30 & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}.$"
