        ":question/id": "85909f08-7094-52c8-bf85-b4e47bc2b8a0",
        ":question/problem": "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}3{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-8)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9{r}^{2}-4{r}^{2}-24 \\\\  & =5{r}^{2}-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 5{r}^{2}-24 & =0 \\\\ 5{r}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{24}{5} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}.$"
