        ":question/id": "ff91a7cd-801d-551f-898a-f82e597274c3",
        ":question/problem": "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}4{r}^{2} \\\\ -3 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r>0$, find the value of $r.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-10)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12{r}^{2}-6{r}^{2}-20 \\\\  & =6{r}^{2}-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 6{r}^{2}-20 & =0 \\\\ 6{r}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{10}{3} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $r>0.$ Therefore, $r=\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}.$"
